        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69611,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous papillomas are localized in the bladder and urethra.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69612,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "<p>Squamous papillomas generally occur in elderly people. Patients may be asymptomatic or present with gross haematuria, urinary frequency, urgency, or dysuria {24159399}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-11T17:12:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69613,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69614,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "<p>Squamous papillomas occur in patients of various ages (range: 27&ndash;84&nbsp;years; median: 62&nbsp;years) The M:F&nbsp;ratio is 3:2 {10738227; 16819332}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-11T17:12:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69615,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "<p>The pathogenesis of squamous papilloma is unknown. It is not related to HPV infection {10738227}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-11T17:13:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69616,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours appear as exophytic, tan-white lesions that arise from the urothelium. On endoscopic examination, they can be clinically suspicious for malignancy {24159399}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69617,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p>Squamous papilloma consists of papillary projections containing fibrovascular cores covered by benign, keratinizing squamous epithelium. The neoplastic cells are positive for p63 and negative for CK7 and CK20. Ki-67 expression is limited to the basal cells, and p53 shows wildtype expression {24159399; 10738227}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-03-11T17:13:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69618,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "<p>Not relevant</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-01T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69619,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous papilloma usually shows a diploid pattern with undetectable or minimal nuclear p53 accumulation. EGFR protein expression has been reported {16819332}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69620,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a papillary growth with fibrovascular cores lined by squamous epithelium; squamous mucosa shows no architectural or cytological atypia.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> negative for HPV infection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69621,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69622,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 79,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign lesions that typically resolve with complete endoscopic resection and have infrequent recurrence {10738227; 16819332}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
